  "limitations": [
    "Specific pictured surviving West Mebon: three distinct east-wall gateways (one lower broken crown), capped perforated east wall, mapped narrow east-to-central stone causeway and low square central platform, sparse low north/west/south ruin fragments. Keep mapped pool open and native reservoir/ground unchanged. No restored complete four-sided temple, museum Vishnu statue, invented roofed central shrine, copied sculpture or photo atlas.",
    "Standard PMTiles named Prasat Mebon Khang Lech/West Mebon POI52776565116292 and water POI35184706717784 correlate candidateQ599465. The matching building record52776565116292 incorrectly covers the island embankment and pool; use its inner98x100m pool boundary plus east-west bridged path35185367201669 for layout, not its222x185m outer landmass as a roof. Anchor103.80011111,13.43463611; heading0/native east-south axes. East gateways nearx63.1, z0.2/49.5/99.2; causeway follows native path from[61.471,48.773] to[13.843,48.483]. Facing approximately east-west. Exact individual tower foundations are not separately mapped.",
